Package: clearpower
Version: @VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: 李皓辰 <haochenli@pku.edu.cn>
Homepage: https://github.com/Clearailhc/ClearPower
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-gi, gir1.2-glib-2.0, python3-psutil, gnome-shell (>= 48), polkitd | policykit-1, dbus, systemd
Recommends: power-profiles-daemon
Description: Battery charge control and live power-flow monitor for laptops
 ClearPower shows your laptop's live power draw in the GNOME top bar and lets
 you cap the battery charge level, top it up, or force a discharge — in the
 spirit of AlDente on macOS. A small root daemon (clearpowerd) samples sysfs
 and Intel RAPL and owns the charge-control state machine; the GNOME Shell
 extension draws the power-flow diagram and controls.
